title: "skill-upgrade: a repeatable process for taking a behavioral skill to publish-grade"
abstract: "A seven-step process for upgrading an existing behavioral skill for AI assistants from working to publish-grade and beyond. Distilled from a real upgrade (what-for-and-how v2 to v3.1). Steps: spec the gap and lock the architecture before writing; stress-test at scale with an adversarial council and an explicit cut/keep/fix/add boundary; rewrite and anchor claims in real prior-art searched at the time, never memory; separate the universal engine from context-bound packs; formalize the test apparatus into reproducible fixtures and a regression bank; build contribution infrastructure (template, rubric, CI, validation script) that holds the standard without a human gatekeeper; then audit, version, and package. Two governing rules: an upgrade needs a stated what-for, and the process must obey the discipline of the skill it upgrades. A past-100 percent move makes the skill name its own ceiling and spec the runtime harness beyond prose."
